        ":question/worked-solution": "At a given point, a function $f(x,y,z)$ increases most rapidly in the direction of its gradient.\n\nSo, we compute $\u2207f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at the point $(1,1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2207f(x,y,z) & =\u27e8\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\ln (x^{3}y^{2}z^{4})),\\,\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(\\ln (x^{3}y^{2}z^{4})),\\,\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202z}(\\ln (x^{3}y^{2}z^{4}))\u27e9 \\\\ & =\u27e8\\frac{1}{x^{3}y^{2}z^{4}}\\cdot 3x^{2}y^{2}z^{4},\\,\\frac{1}{x^{3}y^{2}z^{4}}\\cdot 2x^{3}y^{1}z^{4},\\,\\frac{1}{x^{3}y^{2}z^{4}}\\cdot 4x^{3}y^{2}z^{3}\u27e9 \\\\ & =\u27e8\\frac{3}{x},\\,\\frac{2}{y},\\,\\frac{4}{z}\u27e9 \\\\ \u2207f(1,1,1) & =\u27e8\\frac{3}{1},\\,\\frac{2}{1},\\,\\frac{4}{1}\u27e9 \\\\ & =\u27e83,\\,2,\\,4\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding unit direction is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{\u2207f(1,1,1)}{\u2016\u2207f(1,1,1)\u2016} \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(3)^{2}+(2)^{2}+(4)^{2}}}\u27e83,\\,2,\\,4\u27e9 \\\\ & =\u27e8\\frac{3 \\sqrt{29}}{29},\\,\\frac{2 \\sqrt{29}}{29},\\,\\frac{4 \\sqrt{29}}{29}\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the function increases most rapidly in the unit direction of $\u27e8\\frac{3 \\sqrt{29}}{29},\\,\\frac{2 \\sqrt{29}}{29},\\,\\frac{4 \\sqrt{29}}{29}\u27e9.$",
